{"units": [{"id": "τολμάω-word1", "translation": "but I of daring"}, {"id": "τολμάω-word2", "translation": "daring"}, {"id": "τολμάω-word3", "translation": "having shared"}, {"id": "τολμάω-word4", "translation": "having dared"}, {"id": "τολμάω-word5", "translation": "with"}, {"id": "τόλμος-orth1", "translation": "Tolmus"}, {"id": "τόλμος-def1", "translation": "Tolmus, a Persian proper name"}, {"id": "τομαῖος-orth1", "translation": "cut, severed"}, {"id": "τομαῖος-def1", "translation": "cut, severed"}, {"id": "τομαῖος-def2", "translation": "ἄκος τομαῖον [a cutting remedy] a remedy prepared, as τέμνειν φάρμακα [to cut drugs] is said: on which see under τέμνω."}, {"id": "τομαῖος-note1", "translation": "as χαίτα τομαῖος [cut hair] in Euripides Alc. 101."}, {"id": "τομαῖος-quote1", "translation": "I see this lock of hair cut for the tomb,"}, {"id": "τομαῖος-quote2", "translation": "hoping for a cutting remedy for my woes."}, {"id": "τομαῖος-quote3", "translation": "cutting and releasing remedies."}, {"id": "τομαῖος-word1", "translation": "cut hair"}, {"id": "τομαῖος-word2", "translation": "a cutting remedy"}, {"id": "τομαῖος-word3", "translation": "to cut drugs"}, {"id": "τομαῖος-word4", "translation": "to cut"}, {"id": "τομή-orth1", "translation": "cutting, section"}, {"id": "τομή-def1", "translation": "cutting, section"}, {"id": "τομή-note1", "translation": "Of a lock of hair"}, {"id": "τομή-quote1", "translation": "Look, adding a cutting of a lock of hair."}, {"id": "τόνος-orth1", "translation": "rope"}, {"id": "τόνος-def1", "translation": "rope"}, {"id": "τόνος-quote1", "translation": "long ropes of raw flax."}, {"id": "τόξαρχος-orth1", "translation": "leader of archers"}, {"id": "τόξαρχος-def1", "translation": "leader of archers"}, {"id": "τόξαρχος-quote1", "translation": "Why then was the archer-leader so unharmed by the citizens?"}, {"id": "τοξεύω-orth1", "translation": "to shoot arrows"}, {"id": "τοξεύω-def1", "translation": "to shoot arrows"}, {"id": "τοξεύω-def2", "translation": "Of finished speech"}, {"id": "τοξεύω-note1", "translation": "Improperly"}, {"id": "τοξεύω-quote1", "translation": "a tongue that has shot not the right things."}, {"id": "τοξεύω-quote2", "translation": "For us every arrow has already been shot."}, {"id": "τόξευμα-orth1", "translation": "arrow"}, {"id": "τόξευμα-def1", "translation": "arrow"}, {"id": "τόξευμα-note1", "translation": "Improperly"}, {"id": "τόξευμα-quote1", "translation": "Everyone passing by sent a charming arrow of the eye."}, {"id": "τοξικός-orth1", "translation": "of the bow, archer"}, {"id": "τοξικός-def1", "translation": "of the bow, archer"}, {"id": "τοξικός-quote1", "translation": "and from the bowstring arrows falling destroyed them."}, {"id": "τοξικός-quote2", "translation": "struck by a bow-sped arrow, the eagle."}, {"id": "τοξοδάμας-orth1", "translation": "subduing with the bow, mighty with the bow"}, {"id": "τοξοδάμας-def1", "translation": "who subdues with arrows or the bow, mighty with the bow"}, {"id": "τοξοδάμας-quote1", "translation": "and bow-subduing and horse-riding men."}, {"id": "τοξοδάμας-quote2", "translation": "and the noble bow-subduing Imaeus."}, {"id": "τοξοδάμας-quote3", "translation": "many men bow-subduing."}, {"id": "τοξόδαμνος-orth1", "translation": "same as τοξοδάμας"}, {"id": "τοξόδαμνος-def1", "translation": "same as τοξοδάμας"}, {"id": "τοξόδαμνος-quote1", "translation": "he brings bow-subduing Ares upon spear-famed men."}, {"id": "τοξόδαμνος-word1", "translation": "subduing with the bow"}, {"id": "τόξον-orth1", "translation": "bow"}, {"id": "τόξον-def1", "translation": "bow"}, {"id": "τόξον-note1", "translation": "τὸ [the] Bothius added. κρεμαστά τόξα [hanging bows] Hermannus."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote1", "translation": "prepare your bow."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote2", "translation": "whether the bow's shot is victorious."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote3", "translation": "stretching the bow long against Alexander."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote4", "translation": "for with the bow no one will approach the woes (προσθίξεται [will touch] Meineke)."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote5", "translation": "like someone stretching a bow."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote6", "translation": "having hung up the bow."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote7", "translation": "equipped with far-shooting bows (thus from the copy for ἐξηρτημένοι [fitted])."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote8", "translation": "famous for his bow."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote9", "translation": "for bows were of no avail."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote10", "translation": "no longer shooting arrows at us with bows."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote11", "translation": "subdued from afar by well-aimed bows."}, {"id": "τόξον-quote12", "translation": "with Thurian far-shooting bows."}, {"id": "τόξον-word1", "translation": "the"}, {"id": "τόξον-word2", "translation": "hanging bows"}, {"id": "τοξοτευχής-orth1", "translation": "equipped with a bow"}, {"id": "τοξοτευχής-def1", "translation": "equipped with a bow"}, {"id": "τοξοτευχής-quote1", "translation": "if you were equipped with bows."}, {"id": "τοξότης-orth1", "translation": "archer"}, {"id": "τοξότης-def1", "translation": "archer"}, {"id": "τοξότης-quote1", "translation": "you hit like a top archer at the mark."}, {"id": "τοξότης-quote2", "translation": "did I miss, or do I hit something like some archer?"}, {"id": "τοξότις-orth1", "translation": "female archer"}, {"id": "τοξότις-def1", "translation": "female archer"}, {"id": "τοξότις-note1", "translation": "There was a play of Aeschylus entitled Τοξότιδες [The Female Archers] (fr. 238-240)."}, {"id": "τοξότις-word1", "translation": "The Female Archers"}, {"id": "τοξουλκός-orth1", "translation": "drawing the bow"}, {"id": "τοξουλκός-def1", "translation": "drawing the bow"}, {"id": "τοξουλκός-note1", "translation": "A word not read in other authors. The noun τοξουλκία [bow-drawing] is used by Constantine Manasses Chron. 3680 στράτευμα βρέμον ἐν τοξουλκίαις [an army roaring in bow-drawings]."}, {"id": "τοξουλκός-quote1", "translation": "trusty in bow-drawing spirit."}, {"id": "τοξουλκός-quote2", "translation": "bow-drawing spear."}, {"id": "τοξουλκός-word1", "translation": "bow-drawing"}, {"id": "τοξουλκός-word2", "translation": "an army roaring in bow-drawings"}, {"id": "τοπάζω-orth1", "translation": "to conjecture"}, {"id": "τοπάζω-def1", "translation": "to conjecture"}, {"id": "τοπάζω-quote1", "translation": "for to conjecture is apart from knowing clearly."}, {"id": "τόπαρχος-orth1", "translation": "ruler of a region"}, {"id": "τόπαρχος-def1", "translation": "ruler of a region"}, {"id": "τόπαρχος-note1", "translation": "where M has ταπαρχος, with the letter ó written over τα either by the first hand or by a corrector. A suspect word, on which we have spoken under ἔπαρχος [ruler]. More fitting is στέγαρχος [master of the house], which Bamberger conjectured."}, {"id": "τόπαρχος-quote1", "translation": "a woman ruler of the region,"}, {"id": "τόπαρχος-word1", "translation": "M ταπαρχος"}, {"id": "τόπαρχος-word2", "translation": "τα"}, {"id": "τόπαρχος-word3", "translation": "corrector"}, {"id": "τόπαρχος-word4", "translation": "ruler"}, {"id": "τόπαρχος-word5", "translation": "master of the house"}, {"id": "τόπος-orth1", "translation": "place"}, {"id": "τόπος-def1", "translation": "place"}, {"id": "τόπος-note1", "translation": "where πάγῳ [to the hill] has been restored from the copies."}, {"id": "τόπος-quote1", "translation": "in this desolate place,"}, {"id": "τόπος-quote2", "translation": "it stands toward the western places."}, {"id": "τόπος-quote3", "translation": "the farthest place of the earth."}, {"id": "τόπος-quote4", "translation": "go quickly from these places somewhere."}, {"id": "τόπος-quote5", "translation": "and every neighboring place."}, {"id": "τόπος-quote6", "translation": "there is an island before the places of Salamis."}, {"id": "τόπος-quote7", "translation": "unless you march to the place of the Greeks."}, {"id": "τόπος-quote8", "translation": "in the places of Greece."}]}